---
import AppLayout from "../../../layouts/AppLayout.astro";
import * as app from "../../../data/app";

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [{ params: { slug: app.slug } }];
}

---

<AppLayout
  title={`Privacy Policy | ${app.name}`}
  description={`Privacy policy for ${app.name}. The app collects no data: everything stays on your iPhone.`}
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="meta">{app.name} &middot; Last updated {app.lastUpdated}</p>

  <p>
    {app.name} is built to be private. This policy explains, in plain language, what the app does and does not do with
    your information. In short: the developer collects nothing.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing. {app.name} has no account, no server, no analytics, no advertising, no tracking and no third-party SDKs.
    The developer, {app.developer}, never receives your data and has no way to access it. This is consistent with the
    App Store privacy label "Data Not Collected".
  </p>

  <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Everything you enter or capture in the app is stored only on your iPhone. This includes your regimen and reminder
    settings, progress photos, side-effect journal entries and adherence history.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Photos taken in the app are never added to your Photos library and are never uploaded.</li>
    <li>Your health data is not stored in iCloud, and photos are excluded from iCloud backup.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Permissions and why</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Camera:</strong> to take your progress photos.</li>
    <li><strong>Motion:</strong> the motion sensors help guide the angle of your photos.</li>
    <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> to deliver your reminders as local notifications on your phone. Reminders are discreet by default.</li>
    <li><strong>Face ID:</strong> if you turn on the optional app lock, Face ID is used to unlock the app.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can change any of these in iOS Settings at any time. Camera access is needed to take photos in the app.</p>

  <h2>Purchases</h2>
  <p>
    All purchases are processed by Apple. The developer never sees your payment details. Pro is available as an
    auto-renewable subscription or a one-time lifetime purchase. Apple's own privacy practices apply to purchases and
    to your Apple ID.
  </p>

  <h2>Exports and sharing</h2>
  <p>
    Data leaves your device only when you explicitly share an export, such as a comparison image or a timelapse video,
    through the iOS share sheet. What happens to an export after you share it depends on the app or person you send it
    to, and is outside the developer's control.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    {app.name} is not directed at children under 13. Please follow the age rating shown on the App Store. Because the
    developer collects no data, no information is collected from anyone, including children.
  </p>

  <h2>Data deletion</h2>
  <p>
    Because your data lives only on your iPhone, you are in control of it. Deleting the app deletes its data. There is
    nothing to delete on a server, because there is no server.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy laws such as India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act 2023, the EU and UK GDPR and the California
    Consumer Privacy Act give people rights over their personal data, including rights to access, correct, delete and
    port it. The developer holds no personal data about you, so there is nothing to disclose, correct, delete or sell.
    You can inspect and delete everything yourself on your device. If you have a question about your privacy, contact
    us at <a href={`mailto:${app.supportEmail}`}>{app.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a new "last updated" date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    {app.developer}, an individual developer based in India.<br />
    <a href={`mailto:${app.supportEmail}`}>{app.supportEmail}</a>
  </p>
</AppLayout>
